Question No: 35. Search Insert Position

The Solution is in C++ Language.

Solution:
class Solution {
public:
    int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.size() - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target) {
                return mid;
            } else if (nums[mid] > target) {
                right = mid - 1;
            } else {
                left = mid + 1;
            }
        }

        return left;        
    }
};

Approach:
The approach uses binary search because the array is sorted. We maintain two pointers, left and right, and calculate the middle index. 
If nums[mid] equals the target, we return mid. If it is greater, we search the left half; otherwise, we search the right half. 
If the target is not found, the loop ends when left > right, and we return left because it is the correct position where the target can be inserted while keeping the array sorted.

Time Complexity: O(log n).
Space Complexity: O(1).
